  "issue_number": 187,
  "issue_title": "pack_submission.py generation auto-detect overwrites an existing submission when a generation is missing",
  "issue_body": "## Problem\n\n`scripts/pack_submission.py` auto-detects the next submission generation by **counting** existing directories:\n\n```python\n# scripts/pack_submission.py:137-138\nexisting = sorted(submissions_dir.glob(\"*\")) if submissions_dir.exists() else []\ngen = len(existing) + 1\n```\n\nThis assumes generation directories are contiguous (`1, 2, 3, ...`). That assumption breaks in two realistic ways:\n\n1. **A gap in generations.** A miner trains gen 2, throws the run out (a normal occurrence \u2014 a bad fitness curve, a reverted config), and deletes `submissions/<name>/2/`. Now gens `1` and `3` exist, so `len(existing) + 1 = 3`. Packing with the default `--generation 0` (auto-detect) writes into `submissions/<name>/3/`, and `sub_dir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)` does **not** error \u2014 so the new head_weights.npy / svf_scales.npy / receipt.json **silently overwrite the existing generation 3 submission**. The correct next generation is `4`.\n\n2. **Non-generation entries.** `glob(\"*\")` matches any entry (a stray file, a `.DS_Store`, a `README`), each of which inflates the count and shifts the detected generation.\n\n## Expected\n\nAuto-detect should pick `max(existing numeric generation) + 1`, considering only numerically-named subdirectories, so it never collides with or overwrites an existing generation regardless of gaps or stray files.\n\n## Fix\n\nTake the max over numeric generation directories instead of counting entries. Repro is pure `pathlib` (no torch/GPU): with existing gens `['1', '3']` the current code returns `3` (collision); `max(nums) + 1` returns the correct `4`.",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-11T08:44:19.000Z",
